1
00:00:00,775 --> 00:00:04,223
Your automation just finished
half of a customer onboarding.

2
00:00:04,263 --> 00:00:05,747
Then billing failed.

3
00:00:05,787 --> 00:00:07,775
So who puts everything else back?

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,685
One business workflow
can touch five systems:

5
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:16,910
CRM, identity, support,
billing and notifications.

6
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:21,435
When step six fails, every step that
already ran has changed something.

7
00:00:21,475 --> 00:00:26,675
Someone has to find out what changed, what
is safe to undo, and prove where it ended.

8
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:29,772
This is REVERSA.

9
00:00:29,812 --> 00:00:32,898
A recovery control
plane for AI operations.

10
00:00:32,938 --> 00:00:36,275
Reversible where possible.
Accountable everywhere.

11
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:41,310
What you are about to see
is the real application.

12
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:43,948
First, live on our Vultr deployment.

13
00:00:43,988 --> 00:00:46,023
A visitor clicks Start demo.

14
00:00:46,063 --> 00:00:50,660
REVERSA opens an isolated demo
session, plans a 10-step onboarding,

15
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:54,625
approves it, and executes
it across five demo systems.

16
00:00:56,850 --> 00:01:00,060
Plans can come from Vultr
Serverless Inference.

17
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:05,310
Here, a plain English request goes to the
model, and the draft comes back as a structured

18
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:08,398
plan. But the model only proposes.

19
00:01:08,438 --> 00:01:13,585
A deterministic policy gate checks
every capability, dependency and risk,

20
00:01:13,625 --> 00:01:17,300
and the provenance shows exactly
which planner produced the plan.

21
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:23,660
Before anything runs, REVERSA
shows what each step will change,

22
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,347
whether it can be reversed, and
where a person must approve.

23
00:01:27,387 --> 00:01:32,360
The notification at the end cannot be
unsent, so it is flagged as irreversible,

24
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,750
in plain sight.

25
00:01:35,875 --> 00:01:37,272
Then it executes.

26
00:01:37,312 --> 00:01:41,935
Each step calls a connector, and REVERSA
reads the system back to confirm the effect

27
00:01:41,975 --> 00:01:48,023
really exists. A green check means verified
state, not just a successful response.

28
00:01:48,063 --> 00:01:51,850
10 steps, 10 verified, 59 events recorded.

29
00:01:53,925 --> 00:01:55,647
Now we break it on purpose.

30
00:01:55,687 --> 00:01:58,872
In the demo tenant, billing
starts returning errors.

31
00:01:58,912 --> 00:02:01,822
After a bounded retry, step six fails.

32
00:02:01,862 --> 00:02:05,910
REVERSA blocks the two steps that depend
on it, and compensates the completed work

33
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:07,372
in reverse order.

34
00:02:07,412 --> 00:02:11,397
Seven compensation steps, one
of them a read-only no-op.

35
00:02:11,437 --> 00:02:15,785
Then the Recovery Proof Engine checks
every effect again. The verdict:

36
00:02:15,825 --> 00:02:17,975
verified with compensation.

37
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:22,797
Don't trust a success message.

38
00:02:22,837 --> 00:02:25,498
Every run produces an Evidence Passport:

39
00:02:25,538 --> 00:02:30,610
a hash-chained record of the plan, the
approval, every action and every reversal

40
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:33,998
. Export it, and anyone
can verify it offline.

41
00:02:34,038 --> 00:02:35,697
Eighty one events, valid.

42
00:02:35,737 --> 00:02:39,850
Anchor the count and the head hash,
and truncation is ruled out too.

43
00:02:42,375 --> 00:02:46,922
The whole platform runs on one Vultr
cloud compute instance in Paris.

44
00:02:46,962 --> 00:02:53,310
The Next.js console, the FastAPI workflow
engine, Postgres, and five isolated demo

45
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:56,435
stores, behind automatic TLS.

46
00:02:56,475 --> 00:03:00,125
Vultr Serverless Inference
is the optional AI planner.

47
00:03:02,375 --> 00:03:07,085
For IT operations and business systems teams,
the expensive part of a failed automation

48
00:03:07,125 --> 00:03:08,485
is not the failure.

49
00:03:08,525 --> 00:03:12,722
It is the investigation, the manual
repair, and proving the final state.

50
00:03:12,762 --> 00:03:15,385
Workflow engines can retry and roll back.

51
00:03:15,425 --> 00:03:18,160
They do not prove what each
system looks like afterwards.

52
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:23,235
The first offer is a 30-day recovery
audit, sandbox-only, with success criteria

53
00:03:23,275 --> 00:03:27,060
agreed up front, then a platform
fee plus execution volume.

54
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,423
No customers yet.

55
00:03:28,463 --> 00:03:30,575
That pilot is how we earn them.

56
00:03:32,355 --> 00:03:36,352
Typed compensation.
Verification after every effect.

57
00:03:36,392 --> 00:03:38,878
Uncertain outcomes kept uncertain.

58
00:03:38,918 --> 00:03:41,915
AI planning separated from authorization.

59
00:03:41,955 --> 00:03:43,978
And evidence anyone can check.

60
00:03:44,018 --> 00:03:45,655
One control layer.

61
00:03:47,855 --> 00:03:51,955
REVERSA. Reversible where
possible. Accountable everywhere.

